## 📖 API Reference

```ts
class MajikMoney {

  // Construction
  static zero(currencyCode)
  static fromMinor(minor, currencyCode)
  static fromMajor(amount, currencyCode, rounding?)
  static parseFromJSON(data)

  // Representation
  toMinor()
  toMinorDecimal()
  toMinorString()
  toMinorBigInt()

  toMajor()
  toMajorDecimal()
  toMajorString(dp?, rounding?)

  toString()
  toCanonicalString()
  toJSON()
  format(locale?)

  // Arithmetic
  add(other)
  subtract(other, min?, max?)
  multiply(factor, rounding?)
  divide(divisor, rounding?)

  multiplyDecimal(factor)
  divideDecimal(divisor)

  invertDivide(dividend, rounding?)
  ratio(other)
  compound(rate, periods, rounding?)

  // Percentage
  percentage(rate, rounding?)
  addPercentage(rate, rounding?)
  subtractPercentage(rate, rounding?)
  removePercentage(rate, rounding?)
  percentageOf(total)

  // Pricing mathematics
  discount(rate, rounding?)
  discountAmount(rate, rounding?)
  markup(rate, rounding?)
  markupAmount(rate, rounding?)

  // Tax/fee mathematics
  tax(rate, rounding?)
  taxInclusive(rate, rounding?)
  taxExclusive(rate, rounding?)
  taxComponent(rate, rounding?)
  feePercentage(rate, rounding?)
  feeAmount(flatFee)

  // Allocation
  allocate(ratios)
  allocatePercentages(percentages, tolerance?)
  evenSplit(parts)

  // Rounding
  round(rounding?)
  roundTo(increment, rounding?)
  cashRound(rounding?)

  // Comparison
  equals(other)
  equalsWithin(other, toleranceMinorUnits?)
  compare(other)

  greaterThan(other)
  greaterThanOrEqual(other)
  lessThan(other)
  lessThanOrEqual(other)

  // Sign
  isZero()
  isPositive()
  isNegative()
  isNonPositive()
  isNonNegative()
  sign()

  negate()
  abs()

  // Bounds
  min(other)
  max(other)
  clamp(min, max)

  // Currency
  isSameCurrency(other)
  convert(rate, targetCurrency, rounding?)
  convertFromQuoted(quotedRate, targetCurrency, rounding?)

  // Statistics (static)
  static sum(values)
  static average(values)
  static weightedAverage(values, weights)
  static median(values)
  static min(values)
  static max(values)
  static variance(values)
  static standardDeviation(values)
}

function serializeMoney(obj)
function deserializeMoney(obj)
```

---

## Use Cases

- Accounting and ledger operations with exact arithmetic.
- Point-of-sale and e-commerce pricing: discounts, markups, tax-inclusive/exclusive totals.
- Currency conversion for fintech or e-commerce apps.
- Payroll, expense splitting, and revenue-share allocation.
- Budgeting and expense tracking with precise calculations.
- Financial dashboards or calculators.
- Simulations for investments or payments over time.

## Best Practices

- Always use `MajikMoney` objects instead of raw numbers for calculations.
- Avoid mixing currencies without an explicit conversion rate — cross-currency operations throw by design.
- Serialize with `toJSON()` for storage and communication; use `toCanonicalString()` for logs and cache keys.
- Use chainable operations for concise and readable code.
- Prefer `toMajor()` / `format()` for display to users, and `toMinor()` / `toMinorBigInt()` for storage or calculations.
- Use the tax/pricing-specific methods (`taxInclusive`, `taxExclusive`, `discount`, `markup`, ...) over raw `addPercentage`/`subtractPercentage` where they apply — the intent is clearer and harder to get backwards.

